That is doubtful. After the piece of foam fell over the last shuttle flight, most EVAs are on hold unless absolutely necessary.

You may consider that last flight as the final flight of a Space Shuttle. Manned spaceflight is at a crossroads of using dated launch platforms and the inertia of the US not using the Russian hardware. 

Since there is really no gurantee that foam won't stay on the cryogenic exterior tank, NASA won't launch.

